d the Ottoman Empire.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/italy"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/italy.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Italy</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Italy is a peninsula and country in southern Europe, the homeland of the Roman Empire.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/itchan-kala"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/itchan-kala.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Itchan Kala</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Itchan Kala is the walled inner town of Khiva in Uzbekistan, the historic core of the city and the seat of the khans of Khiva.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/ithaca"><span class="enc-name">Ithaca</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Ithaca is a small Ionian island off the west coast of Greece, between Cephalonia and the mainland, famed as the home of Odysseus in Homer's Odyssey.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/ithaque-department"><span class="enc-name">Ithaque (department)</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Ithaque was a French department created in 1797 from the central Ionian Islands, formerly Venetian, after the Treaty of Campo Formio.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/itjtawy"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/itjtawy.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Itjtawy</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Itjtawy, short for Amenemhat-itj-tawy, 'Amenemhat seizes the Two Lands', was the royal capital of Egypt in the Twelfth and Thirteenth Dynasties.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ito-hirobumi"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/ito-hirobumi.jpg" 